    13	# Design analysis for the fused variant:
    14	# - Concrete behavior: keep the original reachability test and distance ranking, but expose the
    15	#   decision in the output. Example: if three maroon tokens can be reached from the 3x3 target
    16	#   block and two are trapped behind magenta walls, then the output shows three maroons inside
    17	#   the destination, three gray source traces at the reachable source cells, and two blue marks
    18	#   at the unreachable cells. Relative to the base task, only the classification colors change;
    19	#   the ranking and fill order stay the same.
    20	# - Complexity calibration: the variant uses exactly two added colors, gray(5) and blue(1).
    21	#   This is enough to make the fusion visible without introducing ambiguous many-to-many maps.
    22	#   Every generated example contains all three cues simultaneously: destination maroons,
    23	#   gray reachable traces, and blue unreachable markers.
    24	# - Hidden-assumption audit: the original solver inferred floor/wall colors from local context.
    25	#   That becomes brittle once the output introduces extra recolor states, so this variant fixes
    26	#   the task palette to the spec values used by the generator: floor=7, wall=6, dest=3, center=2,
    27	#   maroon=9, trace=5, unreachable=1. The solver still only reads original input colors.
    28	# - Placement legality: the generator keeps the 3x3 destination centered at (5,5), places source
    29	#   maroons only on floor cells outside that block, and adds a separate sealed 4x4 wall pocket in
    30	#   one corner so at least one unreachable maroon can always be placed without overlap.
    31	# - Visual observability and neatness: the gray traces stay exactly at reachable source positions,
    32	#   while blue markers remain inside an isolated walled pocket or another disconnected region.
    33	#   Because the destination block is spatially distinct from both kinds of outside evidence, the
    34	#   three signals do not visually collide.
    35	# - Generator guarantee for full traceability: we cap reachable source count at the destination
    36	#   capacity, so every reachable maroon is one of the collected tokens. That avoids leftover
